---
description: Cold path anti-enterprise, flat handlers, no Provider layers
globs: internal/notify/**, internal/payment/**, internal/ledger/**, internal/costsync/**, internal/controlplane/**, internal/identity/**, internal/fraud/**, pkg/coldpath/**, cmd/control/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Cold path = stdlib HTTP, Postgres transactions, outbox, webhooks, background pollers. Not `/track` or gnet (see `hot-path.mdc`). Overrides generic abstraction defaults in `code-style.mdc`.

Forbidden: Clean/hexagonal ceremony, GoF Provider/Factory/Strategy maps, single-impl interfaces, `map[string]any` JSON builders, `dto/`/`mappers/`/`usecase/` trees, mock scaffolding unless user asks.

Allowed: sqlc `db.Queries` called directly; flat `Service` struct with pool+cfg; `*_worker.go` pollers started from `main` or `OpenModule.StartWorkers`; `context.Context` on every I/O boundary.

Density: minimum LoC with correct idempotency and audit. Flat control flow; collapse single-use helpers. ~30 lines sequential Go beats 3 files + 2 interfaces.

Provider style (required):

- `SendSlack(ctx, cfg, breaker, recipient, title, body string) error`
- `CreateCheckout(ctx, cfg, provider, amountMicro, ...) (ref, url string, err error)`

Not: `type NotifierProvider interface`, `ProviderBundle`, `NewProvidersFromConfig`.

Concurrency: no `go` inside send/checkout/fetch paths; synchronous under `ctx`. Async only via existing outbox/worker tickers at module bootstrap.

Types: HTTP body struct or sqlc row is source of truth — no parallel API DTO + service DTO + mapper file. `coldpath.DecodeBody[T]` into `T` passed straight to `Service`.

Delete useless tests: pure arithmetic, stdlib-only, nil receiver smoke, field echo, static meta smoke, duplicates.

Package layout: `send.go`, `checkout.go`, `service_<domain>.go` — no new `providers/` or `services/` subtrees.

Grep before submit: `interface {`, `Mock`, `Factory`, `map[string]any` in touched package.
